  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis afternoon there is an upper-level ridge over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. An upper-level shortwave will \nmove through the upper-level flow and bring shower and thunderstorms \nprimarily south of I-90 Wednesday afternoon and evening. Due to an \nincrease in monsoonal moisture the thunderstorms will produce heavy \nrainfall. There is a lack of steering flow so the thunderstorms will \nalso be slow moving. This has the potential to lead to some \nlocalized flooding. See the Hydrology section for details. On \nWednesday isolated and showers have the potential to make it further \nnorth but stay south of an Augusta to Great Falls to Lewistown line. \n\nOn Thursday the upper-level ridge remains over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. Another upper-level shortwave \nmoves through the flow. This will bring another day of hot weather \nwith isolated showers and thunderstorms. On Friday the upper-level \nridge remains over North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. \nThis will increase temperatures to well-above seasonal averages. \nWinds will increase due to low-level and mid-level winds increasing. \nThis will dry out the area and bring elevated fire weather \nconditions to North-central Montana. See the Fire Weather Section \nfor details. On Saturday the upper-level ridge remains over North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. It will be the hottest \nout of this forecast period across the area on Saturday with well-\nabove seasonal average temperatures. On Sunday a weak upper-level \ntrough moves through which will slightly cool down temperatures and \nbring some windy conditions to the area. On Monday and Tuesday the \nupper-level ridge remains over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This will allow warm and dry conditions to \npersist. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Wednesday there is a 40 - 60% chance for thunderstorms across \nSouthwestern Montana. On Wednesday there is a 15 - 35% chance for \nthunderstorms across most of North-central and Central Montana. On \nThursday there is a 20 - 40% chance for thunderstorms across North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. On Friday there is a 25 -\n 30% chance for thunderstorms across Southwestern Montana. On \nSaturday there is a 25 - 50% chance for thunderstorms across \nSouthwestern Montana.  \n\nOn Friday there is a 20 - 60% chance for high temperatures of 100 \ndegrees or greater across most of North-central Montana. On Saturday \nthere is greater than a 60% chance for high temperatures of 100 \ndegrees or greater across North-central Montana. On Saturday across \nportions of Fergus, Hill, and Blaine Counties there is a greater \nthan a 70% chance for high temperatures greater than 105 degrees. \nThis combined with low temperatures in the upper 60s to low 70s \nacross portions of Fergus, Hill, and Blaine County on Saturday and \nSunday morning led to an Excessive Heat Watch being issued for those \nareas from Friday afternoon through Sunday evening. On Saturday \nthere is a 40 - 60% chance for high temperatures of 100 degrees or \ngreater from the Helena Valley through the Canyon Ferry area to \nTownsend to the Three Forks to Bozeman area. -IG",
